# Line endings: LF everywhere, including the Windows working tree.
#
# Practically every text file in this repo ends up inside a Linux container --
# entrypoints and scripts (CRLF breaks the shebang: `env: bash\r: No such file
# or directory`), nginx/tmux/DDS configs, Gazebo world and launch files, and the
# whole frontend/gzweb source trees, which are pulled in wholesale by `COPY . .`.
# Enumerating the safe extensions meant every new file type was one oversight
# away from shipping CRLF into an image, so LF is simply the default.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect and skip binaries; `eol=lf` checks out LF on every
# platform. This is committed rather than left to core.autocrlf so a fresh clone
# behaves identically for everyone. Modern Windows tooling (VS Code, PowerShell,
# Notepad) handles LF natively; .editorconfig and .vscode/settings.json keep
# editors from writing CRLF back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch the bytes, even if content detection guesses wrong.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
# Robot meshes land under simulation/models/; binary mesh formats must survive
# checkout byte-for-byte (Collada .dae is XML and stays LF-normalized text).
*.stl binary
*.bin binary

# Squad: union merge for append-only team state files
.squad/decisions.md merge=union
.squad/agents/*/history.md merge=union
.squad/log/** merge=union
.squad/orchestration-log/** merge=union
.squad/rai/audit-trail.md merge=union
.squad/fact-checker/audit-trail.md merge=union
